t and having  some foliage around it and having the  people run it as well as some more  detailing I think it works well enough  and it definitely gets the idea of the  building across  so moving on to what is going to be the  last building of the main street for now  I wanted to finally build a bit of a  simple new urbanist ish row house out of  bricks and again my my main thing that I  kind of wanted to try here was to  combine different sort of washed out  colors to make the bricks look as nice  as I could and not make them too  cartoony like bricks often turn out  implanted coaster but also not make them  to medieval or rustic but hopefully get  the texture just right for that sort of  yeah that muted very contemporary look I  guess and awesome that's something that  I was flying out here and again I'm  trying to make my own window since the  ingame windows didn't have the exact  spacing that I was looking for and that  is basically going to be the entire  building it's very simple and it's very  straight to the point I did want to make  it as clean as I could which is why I  ended up using these stucco pillars  instead of using any wall arches or  anything like that because I want is it  I wanted the entrance be perfectly  square and perfectly seamless with the  toilet but I decide it's just a very  simple building but I think it goes well  for this building goes what for many of  the other buildings go as well is that  they're very simple in terms of looks  but still some of the objects the kind  of hero objects actually make them  happen and they definitely go against  what you're supposed to do with these  kinds of objects in planet coaster I  haven't said it yet so that I would  really love to get into some more like  modern architecture and flowers coast at  some point in the future if maybe at  some point we possibly have some glass  pieces like making skyscrapers and stuff  like that is something that I would love  to try and always like to mess around  with a little bit in rollercoaster 3 and  I haven't really had the opportunity to  do so in planners coaster so far but  it's definitely something that I I might  try at some point in the future anyway  we now have toilets in the park and it's  the only pointed entrance  or only point of interest Jesus what  happened to my English but it's the only  thing that people can really go to the  parks and everybody is going to the  toilet and leaving the pike again so  that's pretty 12 and I think that's also  all for the the Main Street attractions  that people can actually go to literally  people are just able to go to the toilet  for this section of the Main Street I  didn't want to break up the other  buildings by placing any facilities in  it because that would sort of break the  perfect sort of clean look that the  building's had so far but I will  definitely feature some more modern or  some more actual facilities in the Main  Street so there will actually be some  info places and some food and drink  stuff but for now the toilet is where  we're standing and that's all I have for  now  funnily enough this will actually be the  only toilet in the park which I was not  so sure about when I finished the park  whether I should really keep it that way  but I checked the guests and nobody was  complaining about the lack of toilets  there were some thirsty people and some  hungry people but apparently the people  are fine with having one set of toilets  at the entrance of the park so I mean I  guess I'll take that I have no idea why  that's even the case but honestly if  they're all served by these toilets and  they're okay with walking to the other  side of the park I'll take it  it's not something I'm going to complain  because it's more or less the opposite  of a problem for my case here so yeah  that's there's going to be the toilets  everybody's going to have to deal with  for the rest of their stay in the park  they're going to probably end up being  the worst and the most smelly toilets  ever  but then again toilets in the theme park  or well actually no they're not that bad  what am i what am i complaining about  the toilets in might with the employer  coverage is bad but placing the trees in  the main street just made me realize how  much trees just make everything look  better and I wish that could be straight  like everywhere weather which streets  around both the sides  certainly there are way too many streets  in this world without trees and that is  a very sad thing indeed because trees  are awesome  what's also awesome is some  around the edges of the building kind of  reflecting the lights that I had around  the observation tower it's literally  just that same kind of theme and  especially if you would be looking at  the entrance at night and seeing the  entrance with the observation tower in  the distance the idea is that they'll  have this sort of matching style in  terms of the lights there we go that  should give you a pretty good idea of  how it's going to look eventually and we  have that interesting sort of neon  outline to both of the buildings which  should hopefully make them fit in quite  well together now as a general lighting  tip and I use this plenty of times  before but I haven't really explicitly  given a shout out before as a little  lighting tip which I got from night II a  very long time ago so if you're watching  this thanks man a very quick lighting  table is that I usually do use the area  lights to light up all of my areas  because they have a light source that  actually extends out of the light itself  so you can use it the very sneakily line  up buildings without actually making  visible light that's something I wanted  to quickly end this video with because  I'm out of the time lapse so thank you  guys for watching and I hope to see you  guys in the next video  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

